  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{a} \\sin ^2 \\theta$<br />then $d x=2 a \\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta d \\theta$<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />\\therefore \\quad I & =\\int \\frac{2 a \\sin \\theta \\cdot \\cos \\theta}{\\sqrt{a \\sin ^2 \\theta \\cdot a \\cos ^2 \\theta}} d \\theta \\\\<br />& =2 \\int d \\theta=2 \\theta+c \\\\<br />& =2 \\sin ^{-1}(\\sqrt{x / a})+c<br />\\end{aligned}$",
